  is that when you're treating the  electron as a wave  you can't really talk about it being  there or there or there because a wave  is everywhere in the volume that you're  considering  and therefore the idea that everything  is very delocalized  is difficult for people to understand  back in 1923 there was a piece of kid  who resembled this that actually gave us  the really the fundamental proof that  electrons had wave like characteristics  and so it was a couple of people called  davidson and germa managed to measure a  pattern just like this that we've got in  here very similar to this and they  realize well hang on that's that's a  diffraction pattern that means that the  electrons must be waves or must have  wave like character
 

